ult":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nclicked comment_image_viewer_close 1167 234\n                                  Text text='商品评价' id='' key='' b=[126,895][350,961] vis=true clk=false bg=#00000000\n10-19 22:16:04.021 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG render indicator 0\n10-19 22:16:04.026 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG render indicator 0\n10-19 22:16:06.547 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG anim 0 -> 1\n10-19 22:16:07.004 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG change 1\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"2055kk","output":"clicked comment_image_viewer_close 1167 234\n                                  Text text='商品评价' id='' key='' b=[126,895][350,961] vis=true clk=false bg=#00000000\n10-19 22:16:04.021 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG render indicator 0\n10-19 22:16:04.026 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG render indicator 0\n10-19 22:16:06.547 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG anim 0 -> 1\n10-19 22:16:07.004 24460 24460 I A03d00/JSAPP: CMVDBG change 1\n","exitCode":0,"inBackground":false}}}]},{"id":"6ad6266eb72f63412bd0ecfd","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":32697},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"e619714a-956a-4818-8d2c-59ccca4c4968","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The VM state looks fine, so the problem seems isolated to CommentImageViewer's @Local state specifically. I notice the builder log for \"render indicator 0\" fires twice, suggesting the builder is being invoked more than once, possibly creating a duplicate CommentImageViewer instance that isn't the one actually displayed.\n\nI'm also wondering if the NavDestination becomes inactive while covered by a full-screen modal, and whether V2 components default to not freezing when inactive -- that could explain the setter firing without triggering a rerender.\n\nStepping back, I'm reconsidering ObserveV2's mechanics: setting a @Local property should call fireChange and mark bound elmtIds dirty, since the Monitor registers at construction and old/new values clearly differ (0 to 1). That should work normally, so maybe the issue is that the dirty flush depends on the active UI instance context, which differs when inside the modal's bindContentCover versus the page itself -- even though closing the modal via the viewmodel's @Trace change works fine through the same mechanism, so there's some inconsistency specific to this component's monitor/dirty handling.\n\nI'm wondering if the component is being treated as inactive -- isViewActive() returning false -- since V2 skips rerendering for inactive components, and NavDestination propagates hidden state when the page is covered, even without freezeWhenInactive explicitly set. That would explain why both the rerender and the Monitor callback fail to fire, since freeze mode delays Monitor execution too, and I don't see any freezeWhenInactive decorator or NavDestination mode settings that would explain this behavior. I also want to check whether my hilog reading missed filtered-out monitor logs, since the animation and change logs did appear but monitor logs under the same tag might have been dropped by flow control.\n\nBut testing the freezing hypothesis: if I move currentIndex into the view model as a @Trace property passed via @Param, and the close action already works by updating a bindContentCover attribute on the page's List -- which proves the page itself isn't frozen -- then the viewer component failing to rerender can't simply be explained by the whole page being frozen, since the page clearly updates fine.\n\nI'm wondering if the modal's builder content creates a detached component whose elmtId tracking isn't properly linked to the parent, or if @Monitor callbacks scheduled via a microtask aren't firing for some reason tied to how ObserveV2 schedules dirty updates.\n\nNow I want to verify whether the setter for currentIndex is actually being invoked — logging t