tentCover builders with custom components inside a V2 parent trigger immediate aboutToDisappear. A likely fix is avoiding a custom component inside the builder altogether and instead building the viewer UI directly with native nodes in the page's own @Builder, driven by @Trace state.\n\nAlternatively, I could try ComponentContent with openBindSheet/openCustomDialog, though that's more complex, or abandon bindContentCover entirely and instead overlay the viewer as a Stack directly in the page when visible, handling back-press through the NavDestination — though that changes the original design decision.\n\nThe simpler path is keeping the viewer as a @Builder with state in the VM alongside bindContentCover, since builder-created components get their update functions registered on the page itself, and the page isn't deleted, so updates should still propagate. I suspect the real issue is that when a custom component gets created inside the List's observeComponentCreation2 closure, it's attributed to the List's elmtId rather than the page, so it gets purged when the List's render cycle completes.\n\nI could still need a reactive indicator even with this approach, since the builder content binds to vm.imageViewerIndex and the page's observe scope should rerender that element—unless those elmtIds also get purged like before. Worth testing quickly: I'd move the viewer UI into a page-level builder function exported from CommentImageViewer.ets, matching the spec's requirement for a fullscreen viewer triggered on comment image tap.\n\nThe catch is that global @Builder functions pass params by value in V2 (not reactive) unless using a reference param or the newer makeBinding API. The real mystery is why the instance disappears without a corresponding re-appear—if the bindContentCover rebuilt the content, I'd expect a new instance log, but there isn't one, meaning the native nodes stay rendered while the component instance itself gets deleted underneath them.\n\n","startTime":17