ground placeholder is shown, sized from the w/h values in the image URL.\n- `CommentImageViewer`: full-screen swipeable viewer with a \"1/2\"-style page number and a \"关闭\" button.\n- **Detail images** load lazily via `LazyForEach`, using a data source in `model/GoodsDetailImageDataSource.ets`.\n- **Wiring:** `GoodsDetailPage` adds these to the existing detail list after the service card. The viewer opens with `bindContentCover`. `GoodsDetailViewModel` holds the viewer state, blocks a second open on repeated taps, and handles empty data.\n- **No new requests.** Reviews and images both come from the existing `page/goodsDetail` response, and I didn't touch models, APIs, routes or shared base components. All UI text reuses existing string resources. Every stable id listed in section 7 of [`acceptance.md`](/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26/spec/acceptance.md) is in place.\n\n**Bug found on the device:** when a custom component is the root of the `bindContentCover` content, it gets destroyed right after it's created. The page number then stayed at \"1/2\" after swiping. Wrapping it in a `Column` fixed it, and there's a code comment explaining why.\n\n**What the tests cover:**\n- The review section sits after the service info.\n- Nickname, rating and text match the server data in order.\n- \"+1\" and \"+2\" badges appear where expected.\n- Reviews without images show no thumbnail.\n- The detail title sits after the reviews, and images keep server order and full width, scrolling all the way to the last one.\n- The viewer opens, swipes, stops at the last image, resets when reopened, and shows \"1/1\" for a single image.\n- After closing, the scroll position is unchanged.\n- Back closes only the viewer.\n- Double-tapping a thumbnail or the close button causes no problems.\n- Entering the page sends exactly one request, and the viewer sends none.\n- Going back and re-entering, restarting the app, and fast scrolling all work.\n\n`logs/reports/` also keeps two earlier failed runs. Both failures were bugs in my test script, not the app:\n- The shared harness's `restart_app` couldn't find the app's main ability, so the tests restart the app themselves.\n- My script's count of network requests from the log was parsed wrongly.\n\n**Not verified on the device:**\n- **Empty-data cases:** blank nickname showing \"匿名用户\", no reviews, and no detail images. The public server has no such products, so these were only checked by reading the code.\n- **Request failure and retry:** I didn't simulate a network outage. The baseline's \"重试\" button may not respond to taps, which was already accepted as a risk.\n- **Products with 100 detail images** were never scrolled to the end. The 44-image product works fine.\n- **Emulator DNS fails intermittently.** The tests wait for the network first and record a network failure as skipped, not passed.\n\nAll of this is in [`spec/implementation-notes.md`](/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26/spec/implementation-notes.md) for [`2-submit.md`](/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26/spec/2-submit.md). `git status` shows only real changes, with no build noise."},{"id":"7f37c1bf-1251-4a3c-9204-6446e320f020","type":"TOOL","toolName":"task_complete","params":{"tasks":["e91nqa","tg96tf","g7oq53"]},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"","metadata":{"tasks":["e91nqa","tg96tf","g7oq53"]}}}]},{"id":"6ad63296e2713b7e00ffbeae","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":7797},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"a9d215a2-bd1f-4756-a7f2-6223c557ac33","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"These look like notifications of already-handled background tasks, all showing exit code 0, though the first two runs actually had failures before that — the exit code just reflects the shell's echo. No action needed here, I've already checked the logs.\n\n","startTime":1792422557313,"lastModifiedTime":1792422557946},{"id":"2f0619c5-b8df-4918-be0c-fa9d7cab0b6b","type":"TEXT","end":true,"co